From a361cef25f5fb62a55d5630d1a7ca8a7887cb0a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 19:46:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 076/112] Settings > Defaults > OLED brightness: the OLED's
 contrast in ten steps

The OLED's contrast was set once at boot to 0xFF (oledMainInit(), SSD1309
command 0x81) with no way to lower it. Now OLED brightness (7-segment
name "OLED"), right after Pad brightness, has levels 1-10 for the contrast
1, 4, 14, 29, 51, 79, 114, 155, 202, 255 (1 + 254 * ((level - 1) / 9)^2:
the light goes with the segment current, i.e. the contrast, and lightness
as seen roughly with its square root, so the steps look about even);
10 is as bright as before.

Sending it at runtime: the OLED shares RSPI0 with the CV DAC, its image
goes by DMA and its D/C line and chip select are set by the PIC. The
command goes through the SPI transfer queue as a third destination
(OLED_CODE_FOR_COMMAND, its two bytes in dataAddress), so it never meets
an image transfer or a CV message: oledRoutine() sends D/C low to the PIC
before the selection; once the PIC has answered the selection,
oledSelectingComplete() writes 0x81 and the value with
R_RSPI_SendBasic8() (as oledMainInit() does), waits for the end, sends
D/C high and deselects; oledDeselectionComplete() goes on with the
queue. oledTransferComplete() still chains images only, so a command
waits for the deselection. OLED::freezeWithError() sets D/C high before
it selects the OLED, in case a command was cut short.

Each turn of the encoder goes to the OLED at once; the value is saved
when the menu is left, as the hidden entry oledContrast of
CommunityFeatures.XML (the contrast, 1-255; missing: 255), read at boot
(oledMainInit() sends 255 first, the file's value follows through the
queue). The Deluge with the 7-segment display has no OLED: the item isn't
shown and nothing is sent (have_oled_screen).

Tested in the emulator with the OLED's side modelled (the PIC's D/C and
select, echoes, the image DMA's and the CV DAC's interrupts;
tests/settings/oled_brightness_emu.py): 23 of 23 checks: the command bytes
with D/C low and the OLED selected, never during an image's DMA (also
when turned while one runs), images always with D/C high, the file entry,
the value at boot after a restart, nothing on the 7-segment Deluge.
tests/song demand 87a7df292189e341, digital 4473b3155dcfa0e8 (unchanged);
USB audio setting 2 of 2, CPU monitor shortcut 34 of 34.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
